---
description: Checklist for validating user-facing changes with Stunt Double checklists, workflows and feedback before and after merging. Use when changing user-facing flows, UI copy, forms or error handling.
alwaysApply: false
globs:
  - "**/*"
---

review-checklist:

Before merging:
- Run the Stunt Double checklists that cover the changed flow (`search` with `types: ["checklist"]`) against staging or the preview before merging.
- Verify that existing workflows still pass after modifying user-facing flows.
- Check feedback widget comments on the changed pages (`list_feedback` with `page_path`) for known issues in the area.

Coverage:
- Ensure new user journeys have a checklist, and business-critical ones a guardrail workflow, for ongoing validation.
- If a new user-facing feature is added, check that at least one actor covers the target user segment.
- If no actor exists for the affected user segment, recommend creating one via `create_actor`.

After merging:
- Re-run affected workflows against the deployed environment to confirm the fix.
- Set feedback comments addressed by the change to `resolved` with `update_feedback_status`, once a run proves the fix.
- Confirm no regressions from run history: `comparison.changes` on the latest `get_checklist_run`, and `recent_runs` from `get_workflow`.
